    "title": "Missouri State loses to Texas in women's NCAA Tournament first round",
    "text": "MSUMissouri State magical run ends in first round of Women's NCAA TournamentJay PlotkinSpecial to the Springfield News-LeaderMarch 20, 2026, 6:45 p.m. CTUnfortunately for Missouri State, there’s always a bigger bear. Or in Friday’s case, a bigger Longhorn.On its home court in Austin, Texas (32-3) flexed its top-seeded muscle and knocked Missouri State (23-13) out of the Women’s NCAA Tournament in a first-round game, 87-45.Nothing the Lady Bears tried, not even the pep band playing the “Rocky” theme, phased Texas. Texas opened the game with a 10-0 burst, forcing MSU coach Beth Cunningham to call timeout less than 3 minutes into the game.",
